.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt MAP_SHADOW_STACK 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm map_shadow_stack
.Nd map a shadow stack, which Rach2 never enables
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/syscall.h
.In unistd.h
.Ft void *
.Fn syscall SYS_map_shadow_stack "void *addr" "unsigned long size" "unsigned int flags"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Linux maps a shadow stack for a thread whose processor enforces return
addresses against it, where the processor has shadow stacks for user mode
and the kernel is built with
.Dv CONFIG_X86_USER_SHADOW_STACK ,
as the distributions build it.
Rach2 does not enable the processor's shadow stacks, so on the x86-64
kernel the call fails with
.Er EOPNOTSUPP
before it looks at its arguments, as Linux's does on such a processor,
for a 64-bit and an i386 program alike.
Linux cannot build the call for i386, and the i686 kernel has no entry
for it: it fails with
.Er ENOSYS .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
-1 with
.Va errno
set; the kernel returns the negative error number.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width "[EOPNOTSUPP]"
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
Shadow stacks are not enabled, on the x86-64 kernel.
.It Bq Er ENOSYS
The kernel is the i686 one.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr arch_prctl 2 ,
.Xr pkey_alloc 2
